Recent 2025 work bolsters this: An October arXiv paper on loop quantum cosmology describes a cyclic universe with identical epochs separated by bounces, directly replacing the classical singularity while matching observational data. An August string theory model uses "instant folded strings" for a continuous cycle, avoiding zero-coupling issues and emulating Big Bang-like expansion without a hard start. Conformal Cyclic Cosmology (CCC) updates from Penrose in August-November propose aeons where each "end" (heat death) conformally rescales into the next "beginning," preserving conditions like radiation dominance and potentially explaining CMB anomalies as echoes from prior cycles. Even supercomputer simulations (August 2025) probe pre-Big Bang scenarios, testing bounce viability against singularity.\
