\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Medieval thinkers echoed Aristotle, often tying plenism (fullness) to divine omnipresence. Eastern traditions diverged: Buddhism's \uc0\u347 \u363 nyat\u257  (emptiness) is profound\'97ultimate reality as void of inherent existence, interdependent and open.\
Renaissance/early modern shift: Experiments (Torricelli's 1644 vacuum) proved empty space possible, challenging 
\f2\i horror vacui
\f1\i0 .\
