\cf0 By moving seamlessly from "immaterial space" to "the vacuum isn't empty," I was implicitly adopting the modern physical assumption that there is no true void anywhere in the universe. Space is always "something"\'97a geometric entity, a set of fields in their ground state, a metric, a stage on which things happen\'97even when utterly devoid of ordinary matter or radiation.\
