\f2\i horror vacui
\f1\i0  wins in disguise. We no longer fill space with aether or crystalline spheres, but we fill it with spacetime itself, quantum fields, zero-point fluctuations, dark energy, or inflationary scalar fields. True nothingness is not merely unobserved\'97it's considered physically impossible or at least incoherent within our theories.\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Space as positively existent: Even when we call it "immaterial," we treat space as having properties (curvature, dimensionality, topology, expandability). It bends, stretches, fluctuates. That means we're not really talking about a mere absence or negative concept ("not-matter"), but a positive entity that can act and be acted upon.\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 The "nothing" is always pregnant: Quantum cosmology and string theory go further\'97supposed pre-Big-Bang or inter-multiverse "nothing" still has laws, symmetries, or mathematical structure allowing spontaneous emergence. The void is never sterile; it's always capable of birthing something.\
