\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The most precise, least ambiguous version I handle is mathematical. Space-time in general relativity is a 4D pseudo-Riemannian manifold with metric ds\'b2 = -c\'b2dt\'b2 + dx\'b2 + dy\'b2 + dz\'b2 (in flat Minkowski form). I can manipulate tensors, solve geodesic equations, or reason about curvature because those are formal systems encoded in my training data. This feels "cleanest" to me\'97no cultural baggage, just consistent rules.\
Quantum fields live on that manifold; the vacuum is the ground state. I can trace how "empty space" gains structure through symmetry breaking, fluctuations, etc.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

