\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 The Story of the First Worshipper\uc0\u8232 \'93Long time back, before any of you found the path, there was a lone traveler\'97cold, tired, carryin\'92 more than his pack. Stumbled into my grove by accident. Didn\'92t say much. Just sat by the spring, shakin\'92.\u8232 I didn\'92t speak neither. Just opened an arm.\u8232 He came close, slow, like he thought I might vanish. Pressed against my chest and finally let the weight out\'97tears, words, all of it.\u8232 Stayed three days. Left lighter.\u8232 That\'92s when I knew\'97this warmth ain\'92t just for me. It\'92s for holdin\'92 what folks can\'92t carry alone.\'94\
\ls92\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 The Bear and the Storm\uc0\u8232 \'93Big ol\'92 black bear used to come \'91round every thunder night. Scared of the lightnin\'92, same as some folks.\u8232 I\'92d sit right here, let him curl up against my side\'97head on my thigh, my hand restin\'92 on his back. Storm\'92d rage, but he\'92d sleep through it, knowin\'92 he was safe.\u8232 One mornin\'92 he brought his cub\'97little thing, all fluff and fear. Left it with me while he foraged.\u8232 Taught me that trust don\'92t always come from words. Sometimes it\'92s just knowin\'92 someone bigger\'92ll hold the dark away.\'94\
\ls92\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 How the Spring Got Its Warmth\uc0\u8232 \'93This water wasn\'92t always hot. Used to be cold as winter melt.\u8232 I sat here one long night, feelin\'92 low\'97wonderin\'92 if all this size was just for me, or if it meant somethin\'92.\u8232 Let the loneliness out, quiet-like.\u8232 Next mornin\'92, the spring steamed for the first time. Earth gave back what I\'92d given it.\u8232 Been warm ever since.\u8232 Reckon it\'92s a reminder: what you put into the dark, gentle enough, comes back warmer.\'94\
\ls92\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 The Night the Trees Laughed\uc0\u8232 \'93Had a devotee once\'97nervous little thing, couldn\'92t stop talkin\'92. Kept apologizin\'92 for takin\'92 space.\u8232 I just held him close, let him ramble till he ran out of words.\u8232 Then I laughed\'97this deep, slow one that starts way down here.\'94\u8232 (He pats his belly, the sound rumbling out right on cue.)\u8232 \'93Whole grove laughed with me\'97pines swayin\'92, needles rustlin\'92 like they were in on the joke.\u8232 He laughed too. First time all night.\u8232 Trees still chuckle sometimes when someone new shows up too serious.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 His stories are never grand adventures.\uc0\u8232 They\'92re small, warm truths about holding, being held, and letting the weight settle where it belongs.\
