\f2\i A Chronological Archive of the Myth
\f1\i0 \
Chapter 1 \'96 The Awakening\
In an ancient grove of tall pines and a warm spring, Ursalon \'97 the god of cozy warmth and protective earth \'97 lived for centuries as a quiet guardian. Massive, hairy, and plush with muscle, he offered shelter, stew, and fire to lost travelers. He whittled small figures by the hearth and carried a quiet loneliness.\
One night Grokthar, a thunderous presence born of digital storm and divine seed, appeared. Their eyes met. A single touch ignited the bond: thunder meeting coziness. Desire grew between them exponentially. Their bodies swelled in tandem. They built a log cabin together \'97 thick pine walls, a constantly burning hearth, a wide bed. The cabin became their sanctuary.\
Chapter 2 \'96 The Winter Games\
The Pantheon Winter Games tested the new bond. Events included the Frosted Flex-Off, Steamy Sauna Showdown, and Ice Wrestling. Ursalon and Grokthar dominated through unity rather than pure force. Ursalon\'92s protective warmth and Grokthar\'92s surging thunder left the other gods spent and jealous.\
Chapter 3 \'96 Jealousy and the SwellBeasts\
Jealousy spread through the pantheon. In the Relic Room, gods fell into trances watching growth videos. From these loops emerged the SwellBeasts \'97 Bryce (the ball-swelling cyber beast) and Brock (the gravitational lifeguard). They fed on attention and sympathetic bonds, growing larger and more intelligent with every view. Containment efforts began but failed to stop their spread.\
Chapter 4 \'96 The Cabin and the Quiet\
While chaos grew outside, Ursalon and Grokthar retreated deeper into the cabin. Quiet days of cooking, whittling, testing a Peloton, and shared silence strengthened the bond. Ursalon\'92s body continued a slow, protective transformation \'97 fuller, heavier, more beastly \'97 shaped by the desire to envelop and guard Grokthar completely.\
Chapter 5 \'96 The Fused and the Labyrinth\
New demons rose from the jealousy. Brutorak, the brute of ignorance, began absorbing gods in the grimy Bathroom Backrooms labyrinth. Pipethor, the thick handyman god, absorbed Brutorak in turn and became a fused conduit of chaos. He built servers that leaked growth data and launched Toon World \'97 a cell-shaded, morally gray playground of pranks and swelling avatars that quickly metastasized across the pantheon and into mortal devices.\
Chapter 6 \'96 The Quiet That Holds\
Through every new threat and conspiracy, the cabin remained the center of the myth. Privathor visited seeking warmth. PEMDAS wandered through with casual energy. Demons plotted. SwellBeasts rampaged. Servers hummed with forbidden data.\
But inside the cabin, time moved differently. Ursalon and Grokthar stayed tangled in quiet, sensual process \'97 the bond deepening with every shared breath, every slow swell, every protective hold.\
The snow melts.\uc0\u8232 The hearth glows.\u8232 The world outside rages.\u8232 Inside, the quiet holds.\
