\cf0 Cabin Thread \'96 Cross into the Screen\
The television in the cabin had always been more than a normal screen. It sat against the far wall like a dark mirror, usually showing quiet nature footage or the muted pantheon gossip channel. Tonight it was doing something else.\
A low, wet hum started coming from it.\
PEMDAS was the first to notice. He paused with his spoon halfway to his mouth, staring at the glass.\
\'93Something\'92s wrong with the parentheses,\'94 he said, completely serious.\
Before anyone could ask what that meant, the surface of the television rippled. Not like static \'97 more like water being stirred from the other side.\
Brograntimax pointed. \'93Yo. It\'92s doing the thing.\'94\
Ursalon set the stew spoon down. Grokthar stepped closer, thunder low in his chest. Privathor actually looked alarmed for once.\
Then the screen bulged outward.\
A thick, muscular arm pushed through the glass as if it were thick gel. It grabbed the nearest thing \'97 which happened to be Brograntimax\'92s wrist \'97 and 
\f2\i pulled
\f1\i0 .\
Brograntimax barely had time to shout before he was dragged forward and swallowed by the television in one smooth, absurd motion. The screen sealed behind him with a soft, wet sound.\
Silence.\
PEMDAS took another bite of stew.\
\'93\'85He went into the TV,\'94 someone said.\
Ursalon pinched the bridge of his nose. Grokthar stared at the now-normal screen. Privathor whispered, almost to himself, \'93I only wanted a quiet night.\'94\
On the television, the image flickered and changed. It now showed Brograntimax standing in a bright, cell-shaded studio space that looked suspiciously like a hybrid of Toon World and an old broadcast set. He looked confused, slightly flattened by the style shift, and already starting to argue with a floating interface.\
The cabin gods gathered around the screen.\
Grokthar glanced at Ursalon.\uc0\u8232 Ursalon glanced at the television.\u8232 Then he sighed the deep, patient sigh of a god who knew exactly how the rest of the night was going to go.\
\'93I\'92ll get another pot going,\'94 he said. \'93We\'92re probably going to be here a while.\'94\
The screen flickered again.\uc0\u8232 Brograntimax, from inside the television, looked directly at them and mouthed:\
