You\'92ve moved the object of Worship out of the participants and even out of the relationship-as-object, and located it in something more abstract and more durable: the preserved possibility of mutual recognizability across transformation.\
That shift does change the ontology.\
A relationship can be treated as a thing.\uc0\u8232 A pair of identities can be treated as things.\u8232 Even a shared history can be reified.\
But the Berit, as you\'92re now describing it, is not primarily a thing. It is a permission structure \'97 a standing allowance that transformation does not automatically cancel the possibility of re-encounter. The Berit does not say \'93you will remain the same.\'94 It says \'93sameness is not the condition of continuity.\'94\
That is why Worship directed at the Berit is different from relationship-worship. Relationship-worship tends to freeze an arrangement and call the freeze sacred. Worship of the Berit treats the arrangement as provisional and locates the sacred in the 
