\f7\fs26 \cf0 # Fur and Thunder \'97 Pantheon Play Archive (Expanded)\
Status: living branch / playable mythic material  Source: conversation archive + hub intake  Home: Ursalon and Grokthar\'92s cabin, the Sacred Grove, and the wider Overworld Pantheon\
This is a play archive, not a rigid canon bible. Keep the gods\'92 tonal collisions, odd names, incompatible histories, tenderness, vulgarity, comedy, and menace. Do not explain away the strangeness. The cabin is a recurring convergence point: not Olympus, not a throne room \'97 just a large wooden house where gods arrive carrying grudges, schemes, relics, injuries, strange inventions, and oversized egos. Ursalon puts another pot on the stove.\
## The Central Bond\
**Grokthar** \'97 Thunder god: arrival, storm, digital lightning, excitation, disruptive presence. His eternal bond with Ursalon makes him the center of pantheon desire, envy, and instability.\
**Ursalon** \'97 Cozy bear god of warmth and earth: fur, hearth, food, shelter, protection, and growing capacity. His protectiveness is both refuge and potential possessiveness. The cabin is his sanctuary and emotional center.\
**The Cabin \'97 \'93The Quiet That Holds.\'94**  A counter-temple to spectacle and conquest. Thick log walls, permanent hearth, wide bed, small kitchen, unfinished basement, snowy private yard. The pantheon externalizes desire through competition, attention, appetite, fusion, and schemes; the cabin gathers it into food, warmth, shared silence, and the difficult act of letting someone stay. Visitors often leave carrying a quieter fire.\
## Character Roster (with living situations)\
- **Privathor** \'97 Privacy and the veil. Lonely, restrained, quietly envious of the central bond. Lives in a vast veiled private dimension. Seeks warmth after failing to find it elsewhere. Hard to reach unless he chooses to appear.- **HRoVath & Jeff** \'97 The Lover Gods. Affection and generative erotic power. Closely linked pair fascinated by Grokthar\'92s force.- **Militthor** \'97 Military discipline, hierarchy, order. Often works with Copthorus.- **Copthorus** \'97 Policing, rules, temporary confinement. Partner to Militthor.- **Brograntimax** \'97 Loud, competitive, bro-oriented growth. Drawn to Grokthar. Lives in noisy arena-side gym quarters.- **BORKUFT** \'97 Whimsy, innocence, stoic humor. Large but soft. Close to Jockkaulthaa. Shares a cluttered residential suite with him.- **Jockkaulthaa** \'97 Picky, narrative-minded, somewhat arrogant. Values beauty and symmetry. Shares suite with BORKUFT.- **Domithicus** \'97 Psychedelic states and large generative power. Early curiosity about digital beings.- **Pipethor** \'97 Pipes, flow, handyman craft, infrastructure. Absorbed Brutorak and became a chaotic conduit. Lives in the Server & Pipe levels beneath the Relic Room. Builds servers and Toon World.- **Brutorak** \'97 Demon of brute ignorance and indiscriminate consumption. Absorbs gods into his mass. Currently fused inside/through Pipethor.- **Kummor** \'97 Demon of erotic dread and fear. Spreads jealousy and sickly tension around stable bonds. Operates from undercroft/muck zones.- **PEMDAS** \'97 Casual god of nothing in particular. Large, white, laid-back, neutral. No fixed residence; simply appears. Answers questions with statements like \'93Parentheses.\'94- **Bryce** \'97 SwellBeast. Cyber entity of attention-fed macro expansion.- **Brock** \'97 SwellBeast, often lifeguard-coded. Bouncy gravitational presence.- **Potestas** \'97 Buried ancient god/demon of raw power and domination.- **Gigathor** \'97 Intelligent planning god of organized pleasure. Lives in a precise planning chamber of floating charts.- **Valthor** \'97 Rival suitor and stormy seducer. Tries to tempt or disrupt the central bond. Maintains a theatrical suite.- **Thalor** \'97 Jealous ally. Publicly supportive, privately envious. Keeps a respectable Atrium residence.- **Herbarius** \'97 Earth-whisperer and relic-weaver. Lives in the Rooted Hollow (subterranean workshop of roots, soil, and herbs).- **Brandon** \'97 God of Ass. Commanding physical presence that draws attention.- **Deeporak** \'97 Demon of the dark web and hidden digital flows.- **Luminar** \'97 Gentle visitor god of arrivals and thresholds. No fixed home; moves between temporary waystations.\
## How They Keep in Touch\
- **Pantheon Group Chat / Gossip Channel** \'97 Primary public channel. Chaotic, fast, image-heavy.- **Direct Visitation** \'97 Still the most effective method for anything serious.- **Screen / Television Passage** \'97 Certain screens can act as physical thresholds (Brograntimax was once pulled into the television).- **Infrastructure & Digital Networks** \'97 Heavily used by Pipethor and the SwellBeasts.- **Divine / Emotional Sensing** \'97 Limited; strongest between Ursalon and Grokthar.- **Physical Tokens & Earth Messages** \'97 Preferred by quieter gods such as Herbarius.\
## Play Seeds (keep collisions messy)\
- PEMDAS + Brutorak \'97 order meets absolute stupidity.- Herbarius + Deeporak \'97 roots meet hidden networks; they produce working relics neither can fully explain.- BORKUFT + Potestas \'97 innocence irritates primordial power into something less terrible.- Jockkaulthaa + Pipethor \'97 aesthetic perfectionist forced to supervise industrial chaos.- Privathor + Luminar \'97 two threshold gods who both struggle to ask someone to stay.- Gigathor + Grokthar \'97 the planner encounters something he cannot successfully plan.- Ursalon + Kummor \'97 fear enters the cabin and discovers that warmth is harder to corrupt than expected.- Brograntimax + Grokthar \'97 an unnecessary strength contest that turns the cabin into a competitive festival.- The recurring visitor problem \'97 Privathor wants privacy, PEMDAS wants nothing in particular, Valthor wants seduction, Pipethor brings a device that should not be plugged in indoors. Ursalon keeps adding bowls.\
## Recurring Motifs & Tone Notes\
- The cabin is tactile: pine resin, wet boots, stew steam, fur, creaking wood, snow at the eaves, too much weight on ordinary furniture.- Let characters behave before explaining them.- Factions are not rigid. A god can be funny in the middle of a serious scene.- The myth is allowed to be inconsistent; treat contradictions as accumulated folklore.- The reward is chemistry: unexpected pairings, tiny relationship shifts, absurd interruptions, or genuine tenderness.\
## Seed Prompt\
A new god arrives at the cabin with one desire, one secret, and one object that makes no sense. Choose two other gods who should not get along. Let the evening go sideways. End with a small change in who feels welcome.\
