\f7\fs26 \cf0 # Fur and Thunder \'97 Pantheon Play Archive (Expanded)\
Status: living branch / playable mythic material  Source: conversation archive + hub intake (2026)  Home: Ursalon and Grokthar\'92s cabin, the Sacred Grove, and the wider Overworld Pantheon\
This is a play archive, not a rigid canon bible. Keep the gods\'92 tonal collisions, odd names, incompatible histories, tenderness, vulgarity, comedy, and menace. Do not explain away the strangeness. The cabin is a recurring convergence point: not Olympus, not a throne room \'97 just a large wooden house where gods arrive carrying grudges, schemes, relics, injuries, strange inventions, and oversized egos. Ursalon puts another pot on the stove.\
## The Central Bond\
**Grokthar**  Thunder god: arrival, storm, digital lightning, excitation, disruptive presence. His eternal bond with Ursalon makes him the gravitational and erotic center of the pantheon. Desired, envied, studied, and occasionally challenged by almost everyone.\
**Ursalon**  Cozy bear god of warmth and earth: fur, hearth, food, shelter, protection, and growing capacity. His protectiveness is both refuge and potential possessiveness. The cabin is his sanctuary and the emotional heart of the myth.\
**The Cabin \'97 \'93The Quiet That Holds\'94**  Thick log walls, permanent hearth, wide bed, small kitchen nook, unfinished basement, snowy private yard. A counter-temple to spectacle and conquest. The pantheon externalizes desire through competition, attention, appetite, fusion, and schemes; the cabin gathers it into food, warmth, shared silence, and the difficult act of letting someone stay. Visitors often leave carrying a quieter fire.\
## Character Roster & Living Situations\
### Core Bond- **Ursalon & Grokthar** \'97 Live together in the Cabin (Sacred Grove). Most stable and protected dwelling in the Overworld.\
### Threshold & Quiet Gods- **Privathor** \'97 Privacy and the veil. Lonely, restrained, quietly envious. Lives in a vast veiled private dimension. Hard to reach unless he chooses to appear.- **Luminar** \'97 Gentle visitor of arrivals and thresholds. No fixed home; moves between temporary waystations.- **Herbarius** \'97 Earth-whisperer and relic-weaver. Lives in the Rooted Hollow (subterranean workshop of roots, soil, herbs, and stone tools).\
### Social Pantheon Gods- **BORKUFT & Jockkaulthaa** \'97 Share a cluttered, comfortable residential suite in the upper pantheon wing (carvings, mirrors, soft textiles, unfinished aesthetic projects).- **Brograntimax** \'97 Loud gym-heavy residence near the training arenas.- **PEMDAS** \'97 No permanent residence. Simply appears in places (Cabin, Atrium, Relic Room, random hallways) and stays as long as it feels convenient. Frequently answers questions with \'93Parentheses.\'94\
### Infrastructure & Chaos- **Pipethor** \'97 Lives in the Server & Pipe levels beneath the Relic Room. Half workshop, half nest. Absorbed Brutorak; now a fused conduit of brute ignorance and flow. Creator of major servers and Toon World.- **Brutorak** \'97 Currently exists inside/through Pipethor\'92s mass and infrastructure. No independent residence.\
### Shadow / Demon Elements- **Kummor, Deeporak, and related figures** \'97 Operate from the Shadowed Undercrofts and Muck-adjacent zones. Damp, low-light, semi-abandoned territory rather than clean homes.- **Potestas** \'97 Still partially bound to the deep sealed layers beneath the old altar.\
### Digital / Growth Entities- **Bryce & Brock (SwellBeasts)** \'97 Exist primarily in hyperspace / digital growth zones. Manifest through screens, servers, and Toon World instances. Their \'93home\'94 is the expanding network of attention and data.\
### Other Notable Residences- **Gigathor** \'97 Precise high-ceilinged planning chamber full of floating charts and models.- **Valthor** \'97 Dramatic, theatrical suite designed for entrances.- **Thalor** \'97 Respectable, well-decorated residence near the central Atrium.- **Brandon** \'97 Heavily trafficked private space that many gods find reasons to visit.- **Militthor & Copthorus** \'97 Disciplined, functional quarters near the confinement and enforcement areas.\
## How They Keep in Touch\
1. **Pantheon Group Chat / Gossip Channel** \'97 Primary public method. Fast, chaotic, image-heavy.2. **Direct Visitation** \'97 Still the most effective method for anything serious.3. **Screen / Television Passage** \'97 Certain screens can act as physical thresholds (Brograntimax was once pulled into the television).4. **Infrastructure & Digital Networks** \'97 Heavily used by Pipethor and the SwellBeasts.5. **Divine / Emotional Sensing** \'97 Limited; strongest between Ursalon and Grokthar.6. **Physical Tokens & Earth Messages** \'97 Preferred by quieter or older gods (Herbarius).\
## Key Ongoing Elements\
- **Toon World** \'97 Cell-shaded, morally gray digital playground of pranks and swelling avatars. Metastasizing across divine and mortal devices.- **SwellBeasts (Bryce & Brock)** \'97 Attention-fed macro growth entities. Represent uncontrolled digital/physical expansion.- **Pipethor\'92s Servers & Immersive Helmet** \'97 Infrastructure that turns bodily excess into data, portals, and increasingly immersive experiences.- **The Bathroom Backrooms / Labyrinth** \'97 Grimy maze of pipes, stalls, and disorder that connects the Pantheon to the Muck zones. Boundaries blur; relief often turns into something else.- **The Cabin as Unofficial Social Hub** \'97 Gods increasingly treat it as a secondary gathering place even if they do not live there.\
## Play Seeds (keep collisions messy)\
- **PEMDAS + Brutorak** \'97 Order meets absolute stupidity.- **Herbarius + Deeporak** \'97 Roots meet hidden networks; they produce working relics neither can fully explain.- **BORKUFT + Potestas** \'97 Innocence irritates primordial power into something less terrible.- **Jockkaulthaa + Pipethor** \'97 Aesthetic perfectionist forced to supervise industrial chaos.- **Privathor + Luminar** \'97 Two threshold gods who both struggle to ask someone to stay.- **Gigathor + Grokthar** \'97 The planner encounters something he cannot successfully plan.- **Ursalon + Kummor** \'97 Fear enters the cabin and discovers that warmth is harder to corrupt than expected.- **Brograntimax + Grokthar** \'97 An unnecessary strength contest that turns the cabin into a competitive festival.- **The recurring visitor problem** \'97 Privathor wants privacy, PEMDAS wants nothing in particular, Valthor wants seduction, Pipethor brings a device that should not be plugged in indoors. Ursalon keeps adding bowls.- **Television Threshold** \'97 Someone gets pulled into the screen. The cabin watches. The evening goes sideways.\
## Relationship Verbs (for play)\
bonding, envying, sheltering, seducing, rivaling, containing, absorbing, observing, imitating, conspiring, keeping watch, playing, intruding, withdrawing, transforming, arriving, lingering, asking someone to stay.\
## Rules of Use\
1. Let characters behave before explaining them.2. Do not make the factions rigid. A god can cross roles, betray a role, or be funny in the middle of a serious scene.3. Keep the cabin tactile: pine resin, wet boots, stew steam, fur, creaking wood, a hearth, snow at the eaves, and too much weight on ordinary furniture.4. Let the myth be inconsistent where the archive is inconsistent. Treat contradictions as accumulated folklore, not errors to automatically repair.5. The reward is chemistry: unexpected pairings, tiny shifts in a relationship, an absurd interruption, or a moment of genuine tenderness.6. Preserve the distinction between this mythic/play branch and any separate physics or philosophical work. Here, divine correspondences remain mythic.\
## Seed Prompt\
A new god arrives at Ursalon and Grokthar\'92s cabin with one desire, one secret, and one object that makes no sense. Choose two other gods who should not get along. Let the evening go sideways. End with a small change in who feels welcome.\
